img.com/photo/msid-123029159,imgsize-17190.cms"/></item><item><title>Federal court question Trump's tariff authority; cites limit of emergency law, case likely headed to Supreme Court</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123028321.cms" /&gt;</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/federal-court-question-trumps-tariff-authority-cites-limit-of-emergency-law-case-likely-headed-to-supreme-court/articleshow/123028321.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/federal-court-question-trumps-tariff-authority-cites-limit-of-emergency-law-case-likely-headed-to-supreme-court/articleshow/123028321.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-08-01T00:14:32+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123028823,imgsize-1102283.cms"/></item><item><title>Umrah 2025: Over 1.2 million pilgrims from 109 countries have arrived in Saudi Arabia since June</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123025012.cms" /&gt;Saudi Arabia has welcomed over 1.2 million Umrah pilgrims from 109 countries since June 11, 2025, marking a 30% rise from last year. Backed by 89 new initiatives, stricter accommodation rules via Nusuk Masar, and advanced digital platforms, the Kingdom is delivering a safer, smarter, and more spiritually enriching Umrah experience for pilgrims in the 2025–2026 season.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/umrah-2025-over-1-2-million-pilgrims-from-109-countries-have-arrived-in-saudi-arabia-since-june/articleshow/123025012.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/umrah-2025-over-1-2-million-pilgrims-from-109-countries-have-arrived-in-saudi-arabia-since-june/articleshow/123025012.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-07-31T23:26:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123027334,imgsize-1630904.cms"/></item><item><title>Turkish city calls for help after heat tops 50 degree celsius</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123027113.cms" /&gt;Southeastern Turkey is reeling under a record-breaking heatwave, with temperatures exceeding 50C in Silopi. Residents are struggling with soaring electricity bills due to constant air conditioning use and are appealing for state support. Deforestation and policy changes allowing mining on agricultural lands exacerbate the heat, intensifying the challenges faced by locals who depend on air conditioning as a necessity.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/home/environment/turkish-city-calls-for-help-after-heat-tops-50-degree-celsius/articleshow/123027113.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/home/environment/turkish-city-calls-for-help-after-heat-tops-50-degree-celsius/articleshow/123027113.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-07-31T23:18:06+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123027285,imgsize-1333057.cms"/></item><item><title>'He was doing his job': Indian-origin security guard Ramandeep Singh's killer jailed for life in New Zealand</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123026900.cms" /&gt;Lorenzo Tangira has been sentenced to life imprisonment with a minimum of 13 years and nine months for the fatal beating of Ramandeep Singh, an Indian-origin security guard, in Auckland in 2023. The unprovoked and brutal attack, during which Singh was kicked and stomped, resulted in severe injuries and his tragic death. </description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/he-was-doing-his-job-indian-origin-security-guard-ramandeep-singhs-killer-jailed-for-life-in-new-zealand/articleshow/123026900.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/he-was-doing-his-job-indian-origin-security-guard-ramandeep-singhs-killer-jailed-for-life-in-new-zealand/articleshow/123026900.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-07-31T23:16:23+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123026961,imgsize-58842.cms"/></item><item><title>Middle East crisis: US imposes visa sanctions on PLO, Palestinian Authority; cites 'supporting terrorism'</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123026629.cms" /&gt;</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/middle-east-crisis-us-imposes-visa-sanctions-on-plo-palestinian-authority-cites-supporting-terrorism/articleshow/123026629.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/middle-east-crisis-us-imposes-visa-sanctions-on-plo-palestinian-authority-cites-supporting-terrorism/articleshow/123026629.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-07-31T23:01:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123026678,imgsize-678213.cms"/></item><item><title>Indian-origin Oklahoma doctor Neha Gupta, accused of killing daughter, denied bond; judge says charges severe</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123025229.cms" /&gt;Oklahoma pediatrician Neha Gupta was denied bond after being charged with the first-degree murder of her four-year-old daughter, Aria Talathi, in Florida. Suspicion arose due to inconsistencies in Gupta's statements and the child's autopsy results, including internal injuries and an empty stomach.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-origin-oklahoma-doctor-neha-gupta-accused-of-killing-daughter-denied-bond-judge-says-charges-severe/articleshow/123025229.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-origin-oklahoma-doctor-neha-gupta-accused-of-killing-daughter-denied-bond-judge-says-charges-severe/articleshow/123025229.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-07-31T22:01:11+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123025216,imgsize-30772.cms"/></item><item><title>Trump's envoy Steve Witkoff meets Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu; ceasefire on agenda</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123025004.cms" /&gt;Steve Witkoff, US President Trump's envoy, met with Israeli Prime Minister Netanyahu to address the worsening humanitarian crisis in Gaza, a meeting that occurred after stalled truce negotiations in Qatar. Despite increased international pressure and Israel's efforts to increase aid, humanitarian organizations insist it's insufficient.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/middle-east-crisis-trumps-envoy-steve-witkoff-meets-israeli-prime-minister-benjamin-netanyahu-ceasefire-on-agenda/articleshow/123025004.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/middle-east-crisis-trumps-envoy-steve-witkoff-meets-israeli-prime-minister-benjamin-netanyahu-ceasefire-on-agenda/articleshow/123025004.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-07-31T21:46:46+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="